# Cursor → GitHub: tagged releases only

Failed **Geo Core tests** on `cursor/*` PRs come from **Cursor Cloud** pushing WIP branches. Product releases use **annotated tags on `main`** (`publish-update.yml`).

## Allowed

1. Local edits and **local commit** (when the user asks).
2. **Release push** only: version bump → `git tag -a vVERSION` → `git push origin main "vVERSION"` → verify tag on origin.

## Forbidden (unless user explicitly asks)

- `git push` without a `v*` tag in the same command.
- Pushing `cursor/*` or any feature branch to `origin`.
- `gh pr create` / Cursor Cloud auto-PR for incomplete work.

## If the user says “commit” but not “release” / “tag” / “push”

Commit locally only. Do not push.

## If the user says “tag” or “release”

Run the full sequence in `.cursor/rules/release.mdc`.
